  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to have a shared target relationship with BUD-8 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are engaged by Ent-Gloeosteretriol. This suggests a potential pathway where Oblonganoside C influences Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn affects BUD-8. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking Oblonganoside C to a different target (NCI-H1734, Tyrosine-protein kinase Fer, and PLC-PRF-5), all of which are ultimately targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol and then by BUD-8. The high scores in all paths indicate a strong, reliable connection, though the exact mechanism by which Ent-Gloeosteretriol mediates this relationship remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator in the interaction between Oblonganoside C and BUD-8, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm this hypothesis.",
